cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the associated AppliedMath article and this software release."
title: "AppliedMath LexFlow: Deterministic Lexicographic Flow Allocation on Lossy Capacitated Trees"
abstract: >-
  Exact, reproducible software for deterministic three-stage lexicographic flow
  allocation on lossy, capacitated rooted trees: the closed-form Stage-1 maximin
  guarantee and its bottleneck diagnosis, the loss-aware path operator and its
  equivalence with node-edge balance, the Stage-2 weighted-satisfaction and
  Stage-3 temporal-smoothness programs, five exact rational benchmarks and a
  36-node, 16-period controlled canal scenario, the randomized verification
  suite, the comparison with alternative allocation rules, the perturbation,
  weighting and smoothness-criterion analyses, and the scripts that regenerate
  every published table and figure. The loss operator, the closed-form Stage-1
  value and the acceptance gates are evaluated in exact rational arithmetic; the
  Stage-2 and Stage-3 linear programs are solved in double precision. The
  package also contains a rehabilitation-design module (minimum-cost widening
  and lining) that is not part of the associated article.
